Well, I finally ascended Grenny the Archaeologist.  This marks my second 
ascension in Vanilla, my third if you count Slash'EM, and my fourth if 
you count the time I sacked the Amulet on the wrong altar, which of 
course you should not.

No poly objects, no wish for artifacts, no genocide.  And no polyself on 
purpose, even though I had a ring of polycontrol and many 
opportunities... so I'm pretty pleased with myself.  I REALLY wanted to 
wish for Grayswandir late in the game, but by then I had received so 
many bogus artifacts from sacrifices that I thought it would just be a 
wasted wish.

Grenny went to her reward after the toughest endgame I can imagine, in 
which I did practically everything wrong, but through supreme luck and a 
little bit of brains (but not much) made it anyway...

I'll write this in whatever order I remember stuff... so I'll start with 
the endgame.

I was underprepared in several important ways, but I had had this 
character sitting at the vibrating square level for about two weeks, and 
finally decided to just do it... (this may sound like what happened with 
Misery the Valkyrie).  I was planning on doing a lot more sacking (I 
really wanted Grayswandir!), improving my armor class, spending my last 
few wishes on some stuff I somehow missed (rings of lev and free action 
and a t-shirt leap to mind).  (BTW, ascended wielding a blessed +6 
silver saber in one hand, and my ORIGINAL +6 pick-axe in the other)

But for some reason (maybe that I'm a little buzzed), I said "the hell 
with it"  Just went back up to my stash to get the bell and candleabrum 
and reread my spellbooks, then headed for Rodney's tower.

When I got there, I realized that relying on spells for taking out ;-
types might not work (only about 100 spell points), so I spent a wish on 
a ring of free action.  my /oWishing was now (1:0)

Entered the tower, slew Rodney once, grabbed the book, headed down...

Moloch's sanctum was not too tough.  I used several charm monster spells 
and scrolls of taming... managed to tame quite a few dragons.  (another 
note:  CON 23 meant ten or fifteen HP every couple of turns... and about 
350 max from lots of alchemy)...

I wanted to fool around with the Book of the Dead.  I seem to recall 
that it tames undead or something like that.  But I didn't wind up 
getting a chance to try it.  So I wound up ascending with it, though 
I've left it behind other times.  Surprise!  It added like 25000 points 
to my score!  I thought the Invocation Artifacts were useless after you 
get the amulet.

Anwyay, got out of the Sanctum and made it back up to Valley of the 
Dead.  This is where my troubles began.  I had levitated across 
Juiblex's Swamp, and then when the Wiz appeared, I realized I had 
forgotten to swap back to my boots of speed from my boots of levitation.

Oh man... do NOT rely on boots to get you through... I needed that speed 
so bad...

So, levitating, I start firing my /oDeath... Miss... Miss... Miss... 
Miss...

yep.  Four times I missed.  And me with a Dex of 25!  And that was all 
for that wand!  I had another one, but didn't know how many charges it 
had, and had no ID (never found the spellbook).  I started going toe-to-
toe with Rodney... he doubletroubled, of course, and also summoned some 
other nasties.  After taking a beating, I charmed most of his pets.  
Took out Rodney1 with my saber and awesome pickaxe.  Rodney2 immediately 
summoned Rodney3.

<groan>

I managed to take them both out...I think i ZOTted two or three more 
times while doing so... I was now down to a few charges of death, and I 
hadn't even escaped the Dungeons.  But I was safe for the moment, so I 
read my only b?oCharging on the first wand... got four more ZOTs now.

Back through the dungeons, had to fight Rodney a couple more times, 
usually the hard way.  But he's not really tough if he doesn't double up 
on you, and most of his curses missed their mark.

Come to think of it, I fought a LOT of liches too, and barely got 
anything cursed.  The RNG was smiling on me in that respect, at least.

So I made it out of the dungeon.  Had three (not four) scrolls of gold 
detect, and spent the first on earth (i had already found several books 
of dig).  Dug my way through with wands, since they're so damn plentiful 
and I wanted to conserve magic.

Air... let me reiterate... YOU NEED THOSE SPEED BOOTS!  It's ESPECIALLY 
dumb to FORGET which pair of boots you're wearing, and have to change 
them while surrounded by monsters... but that's what happened.  As soon 
as I got to air, I realized I was wearing speed.  While I changed, 
monsters began converging on me.

Just thought of a question I wanted to ask about this character.  At one 
point I polyed into a new dwarf, and wound up with 20 dex!  I thought 
dwarves maxed out at like 16 dex!  does polyselfing do something weird 
to this, or am I just totally wrong about the racial maximum?

anyway, I got engulfed about fifteen times by elementals while crossing 
the plane of air.  and without being very fast, it took me about six 
rounds or so to kill each one.  Thank Quetzy I had done all that 
alchemy, because at one point I swapped my amulet of ESP for lifesaving 
with about 25 HP left.

So, yeah, I died on the plane of air, killed by an air elemental... But 
wait!

Finally made it through (thank Quetzy for all those steam and energy 
guys... being inside one of them is like a vacation at Club Med!)  By 
this time I had realized my mistake about the boots, so I was 
desperately trying to wrest one last charge from my worn-out wand of 
wishing to get the damn ring of lev.  No go.

I gave up and jumped onto the portal.  Landing in the plane of fire, I 
suddenly noticed that I was down to about 75 HP again.  dammit.  dropped 
a blessed scroll of scare monster (only one I had!).  figured while I 
was standing there I'd keep trying the /oW.  Nope.

they started beating on me again... does the effect of the scroll wear 
off?  or did i mess it up somehow?  was it, perhaps, destroyed by a fire 
attack?  i didn't notice what had happened to my scroll...

fortunately, the portal was quite close... I levitated over to it and 
went through...

water was nothing... Water elementals are easy, and free action took 
care of the rest.  Although since I had to use the Amulet to find the 
portal, it took a LONG time.  i'm pretty sure Rodney showed up again, 
but I could be wrong.

so I plunked down into the Astral Plane... this is where things started 
to go REALLY wrong...

first, I got myself surrounded by nasties, and then suddenly remembered 
I was still wearing the !@$%#ing lev boots (-1, no less!).  retreated, 
with the aid of some more charming and taming... swapped my boots, then 
just as I got the speed boots back on, who should appear but my favorite 
Rider, Pestilence!  He had come almost all the way to where I entered 
the level, but had gotten trapped behind some newly acquired pets.  I 
didn't want to ZOT my pets, so I tried to slowly make my way to 
somewhere with a clear line-of-fire...

i forget the exact sequence of events... but he was suddenly right next 
to me.  He reached out.  I got fever and chills...

Started shooting cure sicknesses at myself... Damn that Amulet magic 
drain effect!  After five or so, I was out of points!  I managed to ZOT 
him... only to have him come back as soon as I pushed past him!

looking in my bag for another scroll of taming, i realized I had another 
"oLS in there, as well as two diluted potions of extra heal and a cursed 
dilluted potion of full heal.  By this time, HP were low again, so I 
opted for the amulet.  Thank Quetzalcoatl for that, cause I died of 
sickness right afterward...

that's two deaths... and no more amulets.

Took out Pesty again, made it to the middle altar... nope.  Huhetol.  
Spent my last ZOT on his high priest.  Tried to close myself inside to 
rest but monsters kept blocking the door!  By this time I was zapping 
wands of teleport left and right.  Managed to get a spare turn, and 
quaffed my potion of full heal.

<deep breath>

alright, back into that nightmare.

Hey, look who's back!  It's Pestilence again!  And me with no death 
